   "@type": "FAQPage",
   "mainEntity": [
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "How does the price per sqm compare with the neighborhood?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "On 90 sqm built the asking price is about NIS 51,667 per sqm. The Tzukei Aviv median was about NIS 49,000 per sqm in August 2026, and 3-room sales on nearby streets in 2025 and 2026 were recorded at NIS 48,734 to 52,632 per sqm, in older buildings."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Does the apartment have a sea view?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "The broker describes a balcony facing an open green view and presents the building as the first building to the sea. The land between the neighborhood and the sea is covered by plan TA/3700, which a planner quoted by Globes described as buildings of eight floors at most. Check what is planned west of the building before paying for a view."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "How much purchase tax would a buyer pay?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Under the 2026 brackets: about NIS 128,038 for a single-home buyer, NIS 372,000 for an additional home or a foreign resident, and about NIS 13,356 for an eligible new immigrant. This is not tax advice."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "What are the monthly costs?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "A management fee of NIS 600 a month according to the broker. Arnona was not published; at 2026 rates for a new building it would be about NIS 771 to 960 a month, depending on the arnona zone."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "When can a buyer move in?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "The apartment is ready, and the listings show a flexible entry date."
